        "felicity",
        "infelicitous"
      ]
    ],
    "comment": "Printed unmarked; the prose says that even if many people dine in New York every night, this 'would not make the use of too felicitous' when (12) is uttered out of the blue. Ahn's (12) is called Kripke's (2009) example; Kripke prints it as (14) 'Sam is having dinner in New York tonight, too.' (p. 373).",
    "verified": "page-image"
  },
